{"value": {"url": "https://api.github.com/repos/apache/commons-collections/pulls/341", "id": 1066242105, "node_id": "PR_kwDOAAMmGs4_jZA5", "html_url": "https://github.com/apache/commons-collections/pull/341", "diff_url": "https://github.com/apache/commons-collections/pull/341.diff", "patch_url": "https://github.com/apache/commons-collections/pull/341.patch", "issue_url": "https://api.github.com/repos/apache/commons-collections/issues/341", "commits_url": "https://api.github.com/repos/apache/commons-collections/pulls/341/commits", "review_comments_url": "https://api.github.com/repos/apache/commons-collections/pulls/341/comments", "review_comment_url": "https://api.github.com/repos/apache/commons-collections/pulls/comments{/number}", "comments_url": "https://api.github.com/repos/apache/commons-collections/issues/341/comments", "statuses_url": "https://api.github.com/repos/apache/commons-collections/statuses/b0f382576a48e5758b75c7555aeb098b2fb74e05", "number": 341, "state": "closed", "locked": false, "title": "Fix flaky test occurred in 'CollectionBagTest.testCollectionToArray2'", "user": {"login": "Partha-SUST16", "id": 41873352, "node_id": "MDQ6VXNlcjQxODczMzUy", "avatar_url": "https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/41873352?v=4", "gravatar_id": "", "url": "https://api.github.com/users/Partha-SUST16", "html_url": "https://github.com/Partha-SUST16", "followers_url": "https://api.github.com/users/Partha-SUST16/followers", "following_url": "https://api.github.com/users/Partha-SUST16/following{/other_user}", "gists_url": "https://api.github.com/users/Partha-SUST16/gists{/gist_id}", "starred_url": "https://api.github.com/users/Partha-SUST16/starred{/owner}{/repo}", "subscriptions_url": "https://api.github.com/users/Partha-SUST16/subscriptions", "organizations_url": "https://api.github.com/users/Partha-SUST16/orgs", "repos_url": "https://api.github.com/users/Partha-SUST16/repos", "events_url": "https://api.github.com/users/Partha-SUST16/events{/privacy}", "received_events_url": "https://api.github.com/users/Partha-SUST16/received_events", "type": "User", "user_view_type": "public", "site_admin": false}, "body": "### What is the purpose of this PR\r\n\r\n- This PR fixes the flaky test  `org.apache.commons.collections4.bag.CollectionBagTest.testCollectionToArray2`\r\n- The mentioned test may fail or pass without changes made to the source code when it is run in different JVMs due to `HashMap`'s non-deterministic iteration order.\r\n\r\n### Why the test fails\r\n- As the `CollectionBagTest` uses `HashBag` as its `collection` which uses `HashMap` internally and as per `Java 8` documentation, the ordering of `HashMap` is not constant, so assigning the same hashmap as an array to different objects can change the ordering. So when comparing these two arrays with `assertEquals` the test may fail as their ordering can be different.\r\n\r\n### Reproduce the test failure\r\n- Run the test with 'NonDex' maven plugin. The command to recreate the flaky test failure is \r\n  ` mvn -pl . edu.illinois:nondex-maven-plugin:1.1.2:nondex -debug -Dtest=org.apache.commons.collections4.bag.CollectionBagTest#testCollectionToArray2`\r\n\r\n- Fixing the flaky test now may prevent flaky test failures in future Java versions.\r\n\r\n### Expected result\r\n- The tests should run successfully when run with 'NonDex' maven with the same command for recreating the flaky test.\r\n\r\n### Actual Result\r\n- We get the failure:\r\n    `[ERROR] org.apache.commons.collections4.bag.CollectionBagTest.testCollectionToArray2  Time elapsed: 0.025 s  <<< FAILURE! junit.framework.AssertionFailedError: toArrays should be equal expected:<[10, 6.0, 11, 4, Seven, Eight, 5.0, 15, 2, 12, 16, Thirteen, null, , Three, Nine, One, One, 14]> but was:<[, null, Seven, 2, 5.0, 12, 10, 11, 14, 16, One, One, Nine, Eight, Thirteen, 15, 4, 6.0, Three]>\r\n`\r\n### Fix\r\n- Override the `getIterationBehaviour()' method from `AbstractCollectionTest` and return `UNORDERED` in `CollectionBagTest`.",